I have just uploaded Version 1.0 of KBACKUP to sunsite.unc.edu's
Incoming directory.

It should soon appear in /pub/linux/system/Backup/KBackup10.tgz.

KBackup is a powerful yet user-friendy backup system, fully compatible
with tar(1) of afio(1).
Among the many features included are:
	- floppy and tape support
	- user-friendly menu-controlled operation
	- afio or tar format (get afio from /pub/linux/system/Backup/...)
	- optional compression
	- quick tape archive directory access
	- automatic detection of archive format
	- double buffering for tapes
	- high density floppy formats
	- optional public key encryption using pgp(1)
	- ....many many more
	
	Oh, restoring an archive just requires few keystrokes. The same
	is valid for creating backups.

	After having been disappointed with quite some backup programs
	available, I eventually wrote this one on my own (well, it's not
	my first try...). I hope you'll like it.

