UNIX C/C++ Beta testers wanted to test the next generation in interface
development and delivery - DIOSS.  DIOSS is the first Interface Object
Server development system for the UNIX community.  It allows you to
create TRUE X/MOTIF apps WITHOUT linking in X/MOTIF libraries.

DIOSS is both an Interface Object Server and client side library.  Applications
link with the small client side library and send requests to the
interface server via RPC.  The server creates and manages all interfaces
and events so the applications stay small and don't use up system resources.

DIOSS also includes a visual designer called DiossLive.  DiossLive creates
'live' full working interfaces.  There is no painting, run mode and best
of all, NO code generation.

