CD-ROM SEARCH ENGINE

        The most obvious new feature of The Linux Bible, and the
feature that sets it apart from other linux books is its CD-ROM.
Although there are other linux books that include a CD with a linux
distribution, our CD is different in that besides having two separate
linux distributions (MCC and Slackware 2.3 minus any unfree software),
it also has the contents the linux bible, the linux manual pages and
the linux software map on line, each in HTML hypertext and WAIS
searchable formats, along with a preconfigured linux front end to
these services.

        This is a fundamental difference between the usefulness of The
Linux Bible and any other linux-related book.  Finding information in
other linux references is not a problem if you know approximately
where to find it, but The Linux Bible's CD-ROM search engine can point
you to the information you are looking for given some keywords even if
you do not know where exactly to find it, even for words that are not
in the printed index, and it can often find mentions of what you are
looking for that you might otherwise miss.  If you want to try the
Linux Bible's search interface before you buy, log into
bible-demo.yggdrasil.com as "bible" (there is no password).  The
entire CDROM, including a printable version of the Linux Bible, is
FTPable from ftp.yggdrasil.com:pub/cdrom/bible-3.


