		   EMPRESS SOFTWARE PRODUCT ANNOUNCEMENT

		        PERSONAL EMPRESS FOR LINUX


Empress Software Inc. is offering a special release of its software 
designed specifically for the Linux community.  This product is called 
'Personal Empress for Linux'.

Empress Software Inc. develops, markets and supports a line of sophisticated 
data management software.  Empress is one of the most flexible, powerful and 
cost effective development tools available for scientific, engineering and 
business organizations operating under the UNIX family of operating systems 
(32-bit and 64-bit architectures) and MS Windows. With more than 20,000 
licenses worldwide, 10,000 in the United States alone, Empress products have 
proven themselves in the most demanding applications. Software developers 
requiring power over complex information have relied on Empress as the 
foundation for systems in such diverse fields as medical diagnostics, weather 
forecasting, space exploration, flight simulation, and image and voice 
management

DESCRIPTION OF THE PRODUCT:

'Personal Empress for Linux' is designed to be a standalone, single user 
RDBMS development environment.  The current release of this software is 
based on our full function release of Empress Version 6.6 running on 
Linux Version 1.1.  This has been tailored for use as a single user system.  
The following software is included:

    o	Empress RDBMS including Embedded, Interactive and Dynamic SQL, 
	  Host Language 'C' interfaces, Report Writer/Generator, 
          Database Utilities
    o	Empress 4GL with Application Generator
    o	Empress GUI Builder for Motif
    o	Empress GUI 'C' API
    o	Empress Documentation

WHAT THE USER CAN DO WITH THE PRODUCT:

The Linux developer can use this product to prototype, develop and build 
powerful and open multi-media oriented standalone applications based on 
the Empress v6.6 database.  The applications can be character-based or they 
can utilize the power and flexibility of the mouse driven, graphical user 
interface (GUI).  Using the GUI Builder will open up the database user to 
a broad range of available data sources. Once the applications are fully 
prototyped and/or developed they can be transferred to the full function 
Empress database.  The Linux platform will allow for scalability and easy 
migration of the applications developed into the production database 
environment.

The Empress documentation that is provided with the distribution media 
(CD-ROM) is in the PostScript format.  The documentation can be viewed with 
GhostScript (a PostScript Viewer that is readily available) or printed on 
a PostScript printer.  The documentation files have been compressed using 
Gnu Zip and must be decompressed before viewing or printing.  There are 
instructions in the 'Personal Empress for Linux' Release Notes.


WHAT THE USER CAN NOT DO WITH THE PRODUCT:

The Linux developer will not be able to develop multi-client, server-based 
applications from this software package.  If this is the desired use of the 
product or the final product is intended for resale, then the developer will 
need to purchase the multi-user version of the product (which is simply the 
standard version of Empress v6.6 running on Linux v1.1).  The multi-user 
version is available through normal Empress sales channels.  The following 
features are not included with the 'Personal Empress for Linux' package:

   o	Heterogeneous Database Server
   o	ODBC Interface
   o	Shared Libraries
   o	Shared Memory
   o	Math Functions
   o	On-Line Backup
   o	Warm Restart
   o	Fortran (F77) Interface
   o	IQ Report Writer Interface
   o	ESRI Arc/Info Interface
   o	Oracle Interface


