This message is to announce the release of the latest version of the
Linux port of dvgt 3.51l3.  To use it, you will need a working version
of SVGAlib. 

The new features in this version of the Linux port include:

        + You have the option of either using plain vgalib calls,
          which work on almost all hardware, or using gl graphics
          calls, which can be much faster.

        + Scrolling is much smarter.  Instead of repainting the entire
          screen, dvgt will only redraw what it has too.

        + MakeTeXPK is much less likely to get confused by switching
          virtual consoles now (thanks to ashtray for this patch).

	+ The man page has been cleaned up and expanded.

Try this version out, even if you have had trouble with dvgt before.
It should now work on a much larger broader range of machines.
-- 
Rob Malouf
malouf@csli.stanford.edu

