I have ported an audio spectrum analyzer program to Linux, and need some 
people to test it on various platforms.  So far I have only tested it on 
my 486DX33 running Linux 1.2.10, with a PAS-16 sound card.

The program samples data from /dev/dsp (8 or 16 bit linear audio), 
performs an FFT, and plots the result in real time.  There are command 
line options, INI file options, and run-time commands which allow 
modification of the sample rates and display.  The SVGALIB shared 
libraries are required as is a VGA display capable of the 640x480x256 
video mode.  Mixer support is also available.

The program is available at http://bul.eecs.umich.edu/~phillipv/signal, 
or by contacting me at phillipv@eecs.umich.edu.  

Please send bug reports to phillipv@eecs.umich.edu

