I just uploaded the current release of patches for /proc/dev, applicable
to Linux 1.3.3.  /proc/dev is a directory which contains various device
entries.  A shell script is contained to update /dev from it, which
makes MAKEDEV mostly obsolete.  (you still need it for devices which are
not yet contained in /proc/dev) In particular, generating the correct
/dev/fd* entries for a particular configuration is done entirely
automatically now.  Further, lp, ide, console, pty and scsi devices are
supported in this version.

I have only received positive replies after the last release and not a
single bug report, so I consider this patch to be stable.

The newest version of this patch is available via ftp from
cantor.informatik.rwth-aachen.de, pub/linux/procdev.tz.  I can not
announce it each time a new version comes out, but I am trying my best
to keep it up to date with the current kernels, so perhaps you just look
there from time to time.

Michael Haardt (michael@cantor.informatik.rwth-aachen.de)

