	This is an announce for the Nth official version of MD, a device
driver that groups several hard disks or partitions into a single block
device, so it is now possible to have files that grow across devices. It
currently supports a linear mode, RAID-0 (striping) as well as RAID-1
(striping + mirroring). Please note that, although linear and RAID-0 mode
have now moved to BETA, RAID-1 is still VERY ALPHA.

What's new since v0.26b :
	Some changes here and there (preparing things for
RAID-5... ;-). Patched against 1.3.5.

Thanks to:
	All the fine people that sent me bug reports, success stories and
docs, everybody at P7 for friendship, disks, net access and Guiness (FTA !).

Here is the enclosed lsm entry :

Begin3
Title:          Multiple Device driver
Version:        v0.27
Entered-date:   30JUN95
Description:    Device driver used to group several block devices
		as a single drive, whatever the interface type.
		Support for RAID-0 (disk striping).
		Some preliminary support for RAID-1 (incomplete).
                Also supports linear concatenation of devices.
